<title>HONG KONG: Top Glory interim profit jumps sharply.</title>
<headline>Top Glory interim profit jumps sharply.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   7.58	vs  0.19</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	 vs  nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  4.04 loss vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			    138.80    vs  3.53</p>
<p>    Turnover		     727.61    vs  400.11</p>
<p>    Company name		 Top Glory International Holdings</p>
<p>				     Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Top Glory International, controlled by China-backed China National Cereals Oil and Foodstuffs Import and Export Corp (Ceroil), engages in property investment and food related business.</p>
<p>It gave no details on the exceptional loss.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
